Consumer Protection Act, 2019 - Section 39:
If the District Commission is satisfied that the goods complained against suffer from any defect or that any of the allegations contained in the complaint about the services are proved, it shall issue an order directing the opposite party to do one or more of the following:
(a) remove the defect pointed out by the appropriate laboratory;
(b) replace the goods with new goods of similar description which shall be free from any defect;
(c) return to the complainant the price or consideration paid;
(d) pay such amount as may be awarded by it as compensation to the consumer for any loss or injury suffered by the consumer due to negligence of the opposite party;
(e) award punitive damages in circumstances as it considers appropriate.
